cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AI Tab Grouper in your work, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
type: software
title: "AI Tab Grouper: a Chrome extension that groups tabs by topic"
abstract: >-
  AI Tab Grouper is a Manifest V3 Chrome extension that groups tabs by topic
  or task with a chain of three engines that falls back on its own: the Claude
  API with the user's own key (or a proxy set by managed policy), Gemini Nano
  on-device, and an offline domain heuristic. Tab data is reduced to title,
  host and an optional redacted path before it leaves the device, model output
  is validated before it touches a tab, and an optional local MCP bridge lets
  Claude Desktop list and group the tabs.
